      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Alan Fryer",
      "description": "Taith Gerdded Brotest - Protest March Between 11 and 14 February 2008 members of Cymdeithas yr Iaith Gymraeg (The Welsh Language Society) marched from Ysgol Y Parc in Bala to Ysgol Llidiardau in Rhoshirwaun to protest against Gwynedd Council's plans to close or federate primary schools in the county. The march was named \"O Benllyn i Ben-Llŷn\" (From Penllyn - the area around Bala - to Pen-Llŷn - the Llŷn Peninsula).\nAlong the way they were joined by local parents and children.\nHere they are leaving Criccieth on their way to Ysgol Llanystumdwy - the school Lloyd George attended as a boy, now threatened with closure.\n\nThe banner reads \"Cau Ysgol - Lladd Cymuned\" - \"Close a School - Kill a Community\".",
      "dateCreated": "2008-02-13",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "llyn-peninsula-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcku",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/c/k/u/llyn-peninsula-wp/taith-gerdded-brotest-protest--small.webp"
    },
